-- ============================================================================
-- EC4 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Decision Analysis & Value of Information, beginner
-- tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: ONE TREE ROLLED BACK. What a decision tree is and what
-- this engine assumes (three node types, risk neutral, no discounting, ties to
-- the first branch listed, what it refuses); chance nodes (weighting,
-- probabilities that must sum to 1, a cost on a branch paid before weighting,
-- a distribution payoff at its mean, an EMV no outcome delivers); decision
-- nodes (the best branch, the optimal path, a tie, the least bad choice,
-- walking away); sequences rolled back right to left; and the probability at
-- which the choice turns.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. A node's EMV is its value BEFORE the cost
-- on the branch leading into it, and the Decision Tree Builder labels the
-- node value. A reader who takes the drawn node value for the branch value
-- overstates every costly branch by its cost.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A later choice must be rolled back before
-- the chance node above it is weighted; a reader who assumes the obvious
-- later branch values the whole tree on the wrong path.
-- ============================================================================

values ('decision', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-decision-tree-is","title":"What a Decision Tree Is","lesson_keys":["l01-a-decision-under-uncertainty","l02-three-kinds-of-node","l03-what-this-engine-assumes","l04-money-that-is-already-discounted"]},{"key":"m02-chance-nodes","title":"Chance Nodes","lesson_keys":["l01-weighting-by-probability","l02-probabilities-that-must-sum-to-one","l03-a-cost-on-a-branch","l04-a-payoff-that-is-a-distribution","l05-an-emv-nobody-receives"]},{"key":"m03-decision-nodes","title":"Decision Nodes","lesson_keys":["l01-taking-the-best-branch","l02-the-optimal-path","l03-a-tie-goes-to-the-first-branch","l04-the-least-bad-choice","l05-walking-away-is-a-branch"]},{"key":"m04-rolling-back-a-sequence","title":"Rolling Back a Sequence","lesson_keys":["l01-right-to-left","l02-a-decision-inside-a-chance-node","l03-the-value-of-a-later-choice","l04-four-levels-deep"]},{"key":"m05-when-the-decision-changes","title":"When the Decision Changes","lesson_keys":["l01-one-probability-moved","l02-the-switch-point","l03-drill-farm-out-or-walk","l04-what-the-emv-hides","l05-the-published-tree-swept"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
